==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*h₂eḱ-}}
{{bor+|ru|cu|поощрити}}, featuring regressive palatalization across "р" (''стр'' > ''щр''). Another example of palatalization across a liquid is found in the conjugation of {{m|ru|слать}}. {{doublet|ru|поостри́ть|t1=to spend some time sharpening, to crack some jokes}}, which does not feature such palatalization. {{surf|ru|по-|о́стрый|-ить}}. Ultimately from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*h₂eḱ-}}.

Compare typologically {{m|ru|подстрека́ть}}.

Also compare typologically:
* cognate: {{cog|en|egg on}} (ultimately from the same PIE root);
* noncognate: {{m+|cs|nabádat||[[urge]], [[exhort]]}}, akin to {{m+|ru|бода́ть}}, {{m+|bg|подтиквам}}, akin to {{m+|ru|ты́кать}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|поощри́ть}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-поощрить.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|поощри́ть|pf|impf=поощря́ть}}

# to [[encourage]], to [[incentivise]], to [[abet]] {{gloss|to support, uphold, or aid}}

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|pf|4b+p|поощри́ть}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ru|поощре́ние}}

